.TH devin 1  "devin 3000.11.3 (9c803229faa4)" 
.SH NAME
devin \- A fast and minimal agent that lives both in your terminal and in the cloud.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdevin\fR [\fB\-\-prompt\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-permission\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-sandbox\fR] [\fB\-\-cloud\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-print\fR] [\fB\-\-export\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-continue\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-resume\fR] [\fB\-\-respect\-workspace\-trust\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A fast and minimal agent that lives both in your terminal and in the cloud.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-prompt\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Load the initial prompt from a file
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Configuration file path

Override the default user config file (~/.config/devin/config.json).
.TP
\fB\-\-permission\-mode\fR \fI<PERMISSION_MODE>\fR [default: auto]
Permission mode

Modes: "auto" auto\-approves read\-only tools, "accept\-edits" also auto\-approves workspace edits, "smart" additionally auto\-runs actions a fast model judges safe, "dangerous" auto\-approves all tools.
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDEVIN_PERMISSION_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-sandbox\fR
[Research Preview] Sandbox exec\-tool processes (macOS seatbelt / Linux bwrap+seccomp)

When passed, commands can write only within the workspace and granted `Write(...)` scopes, and can read everything except paths hidden by `Deny(Read(...))` rules.
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDEVIN_SANDBOX\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-cloud\fR
Drive Devin cloud sessions instead of the local agent

The REPL talks to `devin acp \-\-cloud`, which relays ACP to the Devin cloud ACP WebSocket. Requires a Devin account (sign in with `auth login`).
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
Model to use (e.g. "claude\-sonnet\-4", "claude\-opus\-4.6", "opus", "codex")

With \-c/\-\-continue or \-r/\-\-resume, switches the resumed conversation to this model; without it the session\*(Aqs saved model is kept.
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBDEVIN_MODEL\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-print\fR [\fI<PROMPT>\fR]
Print response and exit

Runs in non\-interactive mode: processes the prompt and exits. Optionally accepts an inline prompt: \-p "fix the bug"
.TP
\fB\-\-export\fR [\fI<PATH>\fR]
Export conversation to a file

Exports after each turn. Uses a default path if no path is provided.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-continue\fR
Continue the most recent conversation
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-resume\fR [\fI<SESSION_ID>\fR]
Resume a conversation

Provide a session ID to resume a specific session, or omit to select interactively.
.TP
\fB\-\-respect\-workspace\-trust\fR [\fI<RESPECT_WORKSPACE_TRUST>\fR]
Respect workspace trust settings

Defaults to true in every mode. Non\-interactive (print) mode cannot show the trust prompt and fails in an untrusted directory; pass \-\-respect\-workspace\-trust false to skip the check.
.br

.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRtrue, false]
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
Open Devin Desktop on the given path(s)
.TP
[\fIPROMPT\fR]
Your prompt (use \-\- before the prompt)

Starts an interactive session. Use \-p/\-\-print for non\-interactive mode.
